  "packageHash": "+Crq7noipYi1UjWY2bXAP6gnKe7/sgkJmM7QMPX/6ytA1JCyPvJq7hBf79Rw1pmUfSfCYdx+FlHInQfwzIiStA==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 807809,
  "published": "2026-11-27T10:12:24.447Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v5.13.0: the scope validator can know under which modules a scope is read. New IMyIdentityModuleScopeValidator : IMyIdentityScopeValidator, with IsScopeValidForModulesAsync(MyIdentityScopeValidationContext, DbContext, CancellationToken), and the init-only record MyIdentityScopeValidationContext (Operation, TenantId, RoleId, ScopeId, Modules: the modules an assignment of the role is read under after the write, children of a parent module included). With such a validator, AddUserRoleAssignmentAsync and UpdateUserRoleAssignmentAsync ask it for a scoped assignment, and SaveRolePermissionsAsync and UpsertRolePermissionAsync ask it once for each distinct scope of the role's scoped assignments, in ascending order, when the write makes the role answer a module it did not answer before; a false refuses the whole write with PermissionDenied and a new describer message (ScopeNotValidForRoleModules, RoleModulesNotValidForAssignedScope(int)). Every assignment and matrix write of the role then takes the lock of the role's row (an UPDATE that changes no value), before any lock of an account within one call. A validator that implements only IMyIdentityScopeValidator behaves exactly as in 5.12. The validator is registered as either interface, with Add or TryAdd, before or after AddMyIdentity, which registers neither. Two scope validators of different types make the library's registration of IMyIdentityPermissionAdminService throw; a subclass of MyIdentityPermissionAdminService registered by type that does not receive a registered IMyIdentityModuleScopeValidator throws on every add or update of an assignment and every save or upsert of a matrix instead of skipping the validator. No schema change; nothing removed or changed in the public surface, nothing added to an existing interface. The package validation baseline is 5.12.0. Upgrading from 5.12.0: MyIdentity/UPGRADE.md §57.",
